cody_customer: Hey team — hitting a streaming break for a customer on Vercel Edge. Using our TS SDK v1.4.2 (edge bundle). They get `TypeError: chunk is undefined` and the SSE stream stops after ~2 tokens. Repro steps below.

alex_support: Thanks — can you paste the minimal handler and the client snippet? Also which Next/Vercel runtime? edge or node?

cody_customer: Edge runtime (`export const runtime = 'edge'`), Next 13. Client calling our SDK from an Edge API route. Handler (simplified):

```ts
// /app/api/generate/route.ts (Edge)
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
export const runtime = 'edge';
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
export async function POST(req) {
  const stream = await client.chat.stream({ model: 'rw-large', messages: [...] });
  // they try to do Node-style async iteration
  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    // send chunks to SSE 
    // chunk comes back undefined after a couple tokens
  }
  return new Response(null, { status: 200 });
}
```

cody_customer: On the browser side they're using an EventSource poly that expects SSE chunks from the edge route.

priya_eng: This rings a bell — edge vs node stream interop. In v1.4.0 we switched the SDK internals to return a WHATWG ReadableStream (web stream) for the edge bundle. That broke code that relied on Node-style async iteration (`for await (const chunk of stream)`). Node ReadableStreams are async-iterable, WHATWG streams are not.

lina_devex: Common symptom: first few tokens come through (since some wrappers convert a small part), then `chunk is undefined` when code tries to treat the web ReadableStream like a Node stream. Also bundlers sometimes polyfill `ReadableStream` incorrectly which confuses runtime detection.

alex_support: Quick repro checklist for customers: 1) confirm `export const runtime = 'edge'` 2) confirm SDK package version 1.4.0-1.4.2 3) check if code uses `for await (const chunk of stream)` or `stream.pipe()` 4) check for bundler polyfills (vite/webpack/swc) that may inject node-web-streams shims.

cody_customer: Any quick workaround while we upgrade? Can't ship right away.

priya_eng: Workarounds: (short)
- Use the web stream API explicitly in Edge: `const reader = stream.getReader(); while (true) { const { done, value } = await reader.read(); if (done) break; /* value is Uint8Array */ }`
- Or convert the web stream to Node async iterator with a helper: `async function* toAsyncIterator(ws) { const r = ws.getReader(); try { while (true) { const {done,value} = await r.read(); if (done) return; yield value; } } finally { r.releaseLock(); } }`
- Or set the temporary env flag REDWOOD_STREAM_COMPAT=legacy to force the SDK to expose a Node-compatible stream (internal flag available in 1.4.2 builds we rolled for support).

lina_devex: For SSE specifically, prefer buffering/parsing on the edge using the web reader and then `response.write` style is not available in Edge — you should return a streaming Response constructed from a TransformStream that you feed from the reader. Example pattern:

```ts
// edge route: read SDK web stream and re-expose as SSE Response
const { readable, writable } = new TransformStream();
const writer = writable.getWriter();
const reader = sdkStream.getReader();
(async () => {
  try {
    while (true) {
      const { done, value } = await reader.read();
      if (done) break;
      // assume value is Uint8Array chunk with utf8 text
      await writer.write(value);
    }
  } finally {
    await writer.close();
  }
})();
return new Response(readable, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' } });
```

jason_cs: Do we have an SDK patch to recommend?

priya_eng: Yes — we fixed the interop in v1.4.3: SDK now exposes a small compatibility wrapper on the stream and adds `stream.getReader()` for node bundles, and documents the correct Edge patterns. Recommend upgrading to 1.4.3. If they cannot upgrade right away, suggest the web-reader workaround or the `REDWOOD_STREAM_COMPAT=legacy` env var as a stopgap.

alex_support: I've flagged the account and emailed the customer with reproduction instructions and the 1.4.3 upgrade note. Asking them to try the `TransformStream` SSE pattern or set the env var.

deploy-bot: build/edge-sdk@1.4.3 deployed to registry at 2025-11-18T09:42:00Z :rocket:

cody_customer: Upgraded to 1.4.3 and confirmed full streaming restored on Vercel Edge. No more `chunk is undefined`. Thanks all :thumbsup:

priya_eng: Great — follow-up items: add a short doc snippet in DevEx about Edge vs Node stream consumption and include the TransformStream SSE recipe, and add an FAQ about the compatibility flag.

lina_devex: I'll create a quick snippet and a GH gist, will ping #docs when ready.

alex_support: Closing the support ticket once docs gist linked.
